OpenPDF Studio — Licensing
==========================

Copyright (c) 2026 nullskill

OpenPDF Studio is made of two differently licensed parts.


1. The Core — dual-licensed
---------------------------

Everything in this repository except the components named in section 2 is the
OpenPDF Studio Core. You may use it under either of these licenses, at your
choice:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-OpenPDF-Commercial

  (a) The GNU General Public License, version 3 only.
      Full text: LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt
      Free of charge, no agreement needed. Distributing a work built on the
      Core then means distributing it under the GPL, with source.

  (b) The OpenPDF Studio Commercial License.
      LICENSES/OPENPDF-COMMERCIAL.txt
      For distribution without the GPL's obligations, or in combination with
      components that are not GPL-compatible. Granted only by a separate
      written agreement. The official OpenPDF Studio distribution uses this
      path.


2. Source-available components
------------------------------

    modules/rich-media/     SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-OpenPDF-Business

Their source is published, and they are free for personal use. Business use
requires a Business License after a 30-day evaluation period.
Full text: LICENSES/OPENPDF-BUSINESS.txt

Rich Media is currently the only such component. Everything else is Core.


3. Third-party components
-------------------------

Qt 6 (LGPL-3.0-or-later), Poppler-Qt6 (GPL-2.0-or-later, optional backend),
qpdf (Apache-2.0, optional), Tesseract and Leptonica (Apache-2.0 /
BSD-2-Clause, optional) and the vendored nanosvg (zlib) keep their own
licenses.

Note: a build linked against Poppler-Qt6 can only be distributed under the
GPL. See LICENSES/README.md.


4. Earlier releases
-------------------

Releases published before 2026-08-17 were licensed under the MIT License. That
grant remains valid for those releases and is not withdrawn.


LICENSES/README.md maps every path to its license and lists the third-party
terms in full.
